{"id":"u-02c509c5-c278-4b02-8192-0bed682a693a","src":"community","title":"Lean on Me","author":"Pavel Sveda","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/6LA53g-lean-on-me","desc":"This isn’t a plan built in a lab. It’s a no-nonsense, 12-week cutting program designed for people who still want to move heavy weight, train with purpose, and keep muscle while getting leaner.\n\nYou’ll train 4 days a week, with cardio the other 3 days, following a structured push/pull format that pairs upper and lower body movements in supersets. That means less standing around, more work done, and better results. Each session opens with big lifts to keep your strength intact, then moves into accessories that bring the volume and detail.\n\nThere’s progression built in — rep ranges shift, RIR targets adjust, and deloads are timed to help you recover without losing momentum.\nMorning cardio is up to you: 20 to 60 minutes, walk or run, based on how you're feeling.\n\nWhat you need:\n\nA multi-function machine, cables, dumbbells, and some grit.\n\nThe discipline to show up.\n\nThe honesty to train hard, but not stupid.\n\nThis isn’t about chasing soreness or getting shredded overnight.\nIt’s about showing up, staying consistent, and getting leaner without losing what you’ve built.","level":["Intermediate","Beginner"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-15T02:02:34.731Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push Lower, Pull Upper","Pull Lower, Push Upper","Rest","Push Lower, Pull Upper","Pull Lower, Push Upper","Day 6","Day 7"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":2}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":2}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":2}]},{